# Hyrax upgrade code

## Strategy

- **Stay on Hyrax** — extend community patterns, do not build parallel `Scholar::` stack
- **Shrink custom surface** in Phase A before gem major bumps in Phase B
- **Preserve display** of all metadata fields for existing works when simplifying forms

## Layout

- Work types: `app/models/<type>.rb` → Valkyrie resources in Phase B4 (`config/metadata/<type>.yaml`)
- DOI: keep concerns/actors/jobs; port to Valkyrie in B4
- Shibboleth: minimal Devise + omniauth config
- Permanent URLs: `lib/scholar.rb`, `CommonObjectsController`

## Style

- Match existing Hyrax 2.9 patterns until Phase B lands
- Ruby 2.7 / Rails 5.2 compatible until B1 explicitly bumps versions
- Smallest correct diff per sub-phase
- No comments for obvious code; comment DOI invariants and migration notes only

## Dependencies

- Do not add new gems unless PLAN/STATUS approves
- Remove gems in PLAN order (A1 audit before A2 removal)
- Keep `hydra-remote_identifier` fork until DOI ported on Hyrax 5

## Tests

- Prefer **unit/request specs** over new feature specs; `bin/rspec-fast` for fast tier

## Diffs

- Do not refactor unrelated legacy code
- Naming: [scholar-naming-conventions.mdc](../scholar-naming-conventions.mdc)
- Done bar: [scholar-code-quality.mdc](../scholar-code-quality.mdc)
